.Dd October 4, 2026
.Dt MIROTALK-LDAP.CONF 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mirotalk-ldap.conf
.Nd optional LDAP authentication configuration for MiroTalk
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The actual configuration file is
.Pa %%PREFIX%%/etc/mirotalk/ldap/ldap.conf .
It uses the same NAME=VALUE syntax as mirotalk.conf, but variable references are
resolved within this file only.
Requires the HARDENED build and LDAP port option.
Set LDAP_ENABLED=true in mirotalk.conf to activate it.
Disabled LDAP configurations are not opened or validated.
The users file retains precedence; failed local passwords never fall back to LDAP.
.Sh TRANSPORTS
ldaps uses verified TLS immediately; ldap-starttls upgrades before binding.
ldap-plain is permitted only for literal IPv4 loopback addresses in 127.0.0.0/8
and IPv6 ::1. No TLS downgrade is allowed.
ldapi is reserved for Unix sockets and is not implemented; selecting it is an error.
.Sh LDAP AUTHENTICATION
LDAP is an optional supplement to the users file.
A local username takes precedence, including when its password is incorrect.
LDAP variables are read exclusively from ldap/ldap.conf and have no environment overrides.
When enabled, every applicable setting is mandatory.
.Pp
The following settings are documented in the sample configuration and HARDENING.md:
.Bl -tag -width LDAP_GROUP_UNIQUE_FILTER
.It Va LDAP_TRANSPORT
ldaps, ldap-starttls, or ldap-plain; explicit selection required.
.It Va LDAP_URL
Directory URL including the selected protocol, host and explicit port. ldap-plain permits only literal addresses in 127.0.0.0/8 and ::1.
.It Va LDAP_BIND_DN
Restricted search-account DN.
.It Va LDAP_BIND_PASSWORD_FILE
Absolute path to a protected search-account password file readable by the daemon.
.It Va LDAP_USER_BASE
User search base DN.
.It Va LDAP_USER_SCOPE
base, one, or sub.
.It Va LDAP_USER_FILTER
Administrator filter template containing {username}; substituted login names are escaped.
.It Va LDAP_USERNAME_ATTRIBUTE
Attribute containing the canonical unique account name.
.It Va LDAP_DISPLAY_NAME_ATTRIBUTE
Attribute containing the display name; a missing value uses the canonical account name.
.It Va LDAP_CONNECT_TIMEOUT_MS
Positive connection timeout in milliseconds.
.It Va LDAP_OPERATION_TIMEOUT_MS
Positive operation timeout in milliseconds.
.It Va LDAP_MAX_GROUPS
Positive maximum number of relevant groups accepted.
.It Va LDAP_PASSWORD_POLICY
true to request the password-policy control; false to omit it.
.It Va LDAP_SESSION_MAX_AGE
Positive absolute LDAP session lifetime in seconds; the shorter AUTH_SESSION_MAX_AGE also applies when enabled.
.It Va LDAP_GROUPS_ENABLED
true to retrieve LDAP groups; false to use defaultGroups from group-meetings.json.
.It Va LDAP_GROUP_BASE
Relevant group search base DN; required for group-search.
.It Va LDAP_GROUP_SCOPE
base, one, or sub; required for group-search.
.It Va LDAP_GROUP_FILTER
Membership filter template containing {member}; required for group-search.
.It Va LDAP_GROUP_NAME_ATTRIBUTE
Group name attribute; required for group-search.
.It Va LDAP_GROUP_MEMBER_VALUE
dn or username; selects the escaped {member} substitution.
.It Va LDAP_GROUP_UNIQUE_FILTER
Uniqueness filter containing {group}, required for group-search with direct mode or name mappings.
.It Va LDAP_MEETING_MODE
direct or mapped; grants are combined by union.
.It Va LDAP_TLS_CA_FILE
Explicit absolute CA bundle path; required for ldaps and ldap-starttls.
.It Va LDAP_TLS_MIN_VERSION
TLSv1.2 or TLSv1.3; required for ldaps and ldap-starttls.
.It Va LDAP_TLS_SERVER_NAME
Explicit TLS verification hostname, or explicitly empty to use the URL host.
.El
.Pp
Group membership and the complete group-meetings.json policy are checked on every login.
Account and group changes take effect at the next login or session expiry.
Passwords are not retained in tokens or reused when creating or joining meetings.

.Bl -tag -width LDAP_USER_GROUP_ATTRIBUTE
.It Va LDAP_GROUP_SOURCE
user-attribute or group-search; explicitly required when groups are enabled.
.It Va LDAP_USER_GROUP_ATTRIBUTE
Attribute containing group names on the user entry; required for user-attribute.
.It Va LDAP_MAPPING_KEY
name or dn; explicitly required in mapped mode.
User-attribute supports name mappings only.
Group-search supports both.
.El
.Pp
Direct mode treats group names as approved meeting identifiers.
Mapped mode grants the union of meetings listed by the user's groups.
A meeting may belong to multiple groups.

.Sh OPERATIONAL DEFAULTS
Omitted operational settings use these defaults:
LDAP_CONNECT_TIMEOUT_MS=3000,
LDAP_OPERATION_TIMEOUT_MS=5000,
LDAP_MAX_GROUPS=1000,
LDAP_PASSWORD_POLICY=true,
LDAP_SESSION_MAX_AGE=28800 (seconds),
LDAP_TLS_MIN_VERSION=TLSv1.2, and
LDAP_TLS_SERVER_NAME empty (verify the URL host).
Explicit invalid or empty values are rejected except where empty is permitted.
Directory, transport, group and meeting policy settings remain explicit;
commented examples without a stated default are not active values.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "ldap/group-meetings.json"
.It Pa %%PREFIX%%/etc/mirotalk/ldap/ldap.conf
LDAP connection, identity and group lookup settings.
.It Pa %%PREFIX%%/etc/mirotalk/ldap/bind-secret
Protected search-account password.
.It Pa %%PREFIX%%/etc/mirotalk/ldap/group-meetings.json
Default groups and group-to-meeting grants.
.El
.Sh GROUP MEETING POLICY
The file contains exactly defaultGroups (array) and groupMeetings (object).
groupMeetings maps each stable LDAP group key to a nonempty array of exact
meeting keys. Matching uses LDAP_MAPPING_KEY=name or dn in mapped mode.
Grants are the union of matching groups, with duplicate meetings removed.
.Pp
defaultGroups applies only after successful authentication returns no groups.
It never supplements existing membership or masks LDAP errors. Empty defaults
disable fallback. Direct mode uses group keys as meeting keys; mapped mode
resolves them through groupMeetings. Display attributes never affect matching.
.Pp
The complete policy is validated on each login and replaced atomically.
A missing file in mapped mode denies login; direct mode allows a missing file
with no default groups. Malformed JSON, duplicate JSON keys, unknown fields,
invalid keys, empty grants, unreadable files, symlinks and unsafe permissions
deny login. The file is limited to 256 KiB and must not be writable by group or others.
A literal * LDAP meeting key grants only that meeting, never wildcard access.
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
Server logs identify the failed setting, file or LDAP operation.
LDAP passwords and bind-secret contents are never included.
Credential failures use a generic browser alert.
An authenticated account with no meeting grants receives a separate,
localized alert and is denied a login session.

.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mirotalk.conf 5 ,
.Xr mirotalk 8
